    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32666" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕκπλεθρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>six plethra long,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				387
			</span></i> ; in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕ. ἀγών,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάδιον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				883
			</span></i>, and 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶλον ἕ. δρόμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1181
				</span></i>
			 (where Sch. expl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα καὶ
				ὑπερβαῖνον πλέθρου μέτρον</span>) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ.</span> is the better reading,
		<i>narrowing.</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
